        "title": "Trading core efficiency — is the workload running?",
        "type": "row"
      },
      {
        "datasource": {
          "type": "influxdb",
          "uid": "amd_pmu"
        },
        "description": "Rate of instructions completing on each trading core (cores with role=trading, excludes housekeeping cores 0,92-95,188-191).\n\nNormal: 1-3 billion instr/sec per active core.\nQuiet cores near 0 are fine — trading is bursty.\nIf ALL cores stay near 0 for \u003e5 minutes, the workload may have died — run `sudo pmu-core-explain \u003ccore\u003e` to identify what's on each core.",
        "fieldConfig": {
          "defaults": {
            "color": {
              "mode": "palette-classic"
            },
            "custom": {
              "axisPlacement": "auto",
              "drawStyle": "line",
              "fillOpacity": 5,
              "gradientMode": "none",
              "hideFrom": {
                "legend": false,
                "tooltip": false,
                "viz": false
