        "id": 600,
        "options": {
          "code": {
            "language": "plaintext",
            "showLineNumbers": false,
            "showMiniMap": false
          },
          "content": "## When something looks wrong, run these on the host\n\n**Identify what's on a core:**\n```\nsudo pmu-core-explain \u003ccore\u003e              # 30s snapshot + classification\nsudo pmu-core-explain \u003ccore\u003e --duration 60 --deep    # longer window + wchan\n```\n\n**Check current NUMA placement of a process:**\n```\nnumactl --show                            # current process NUMA policy\nsudo cat /proc/\u003cpid\u003e/numa_maps            # per-mapping NUMA info\nsudo taskset -pc \u003cpid\u003e                    # what cores is it pinned to?\n```\n\n**Manual PMU capture (deeper than the 5-min timer):**\n```\nsudo AMD_HK_CORES=97 /usr/local/sbin/amd-perf-capture group_core_A\nsudo /opt/AMDuProf_5.3-521/bin/AMDuProfPcm -m memory -a -d 30 -o /tmp/mem.csv\n```\n\n**Check that the pipeline is alive:**\n```\nsystemctl status amd-perf-shipper.timer   # should show 'active'\nsudo tail /var/log/amd-perf/cycle.log     # recent cycles\n```\n\n**Escalation:** if a metric is red-thresholded for \u003e15 minutes AND you can't identify a legitimate cause, page on-call HW/perf engineer with the panel URL and the output of `pmu-core-explain` on any affected core.",
          "mode": "markdown"
        },
